Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["III.L.6 Why it matters", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"95e2e182-6886-42ea-bbe8-79ea36ab2548"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["It enters no other result.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " The effective Lagrangians of the solution contain the computed function ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[ScriptCapitalV]",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["SF",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["X", "TI"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5547e339-f4cc-43cb-8523-60e868fe5ad2"],
 ", not the Landau form, and no other result uses ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["a", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["SF",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["X", "TI"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "55de8467-c2c3-4ff5-b8b7-4bdf30d2e36f"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["b", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["SF",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["X", "TI"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "295df6de-1fad-47b3-bf13-9840288159ed"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["c", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["SF",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["X", "TI"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "065276e4-aa6e-4058-994e-f99ec2c25c66"],
 ": the mass of the amplitude mode uses the curvature ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[ScriptCapitalV]",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["amp",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[Prime]\[Prime]"], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "9fd66868-7e7b-4302-ba70-8c1a1448b0c7"],
 " of the computed curve, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["u", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["SF",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["X", "TI"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "aca778fa-da53-4dff-a06d-aeaebf0c465b"],
 " and the mass of the non-unitary modes use the computed curvature in the \
non-unitary direction, and the masses of the gauge bosons and the dynamics \
use ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", 
    RowBox[{"0", ",", 
     StyleBox["SF",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]}], 
    StyleBox["X", "TI"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "612f64ef-159d-4c39-9470-9b023d65a830"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["Z", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["SF",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["X", "TI"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1b56f7f6-80aa-4c3b-946d-695942bdc4c7"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["Y", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["SF",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["X", "TI"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c5a439f0-dcb1-438d-ab22-c8d9b8ac3b7a"],
 " and the susceptibilities."
}], "ItemNumbered",ExpressionUUID->"1cf8e223-41b3-4ee7-a40d-7a4351cf649e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["It matters to whoever replaces $\\mathcal V^X_{\\rm SF}$ by the \
Landau form",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ", as in a model of the type of Ginzburg and Landau or of Higgs: the minimum \
of the polynomial is 0.04 to 0.11 per cent too small, its depth 0.12 to 0.31 \
per cent too large, its curvature at its minimum 0.86 to 2.3 per cent too \
large, and the mass of the amplitude mode 0.43 to 1.1 per cent too large (the \
table above). A derivative enlarges the relative error of the function. \
Beyond the fitted interval the error grows: fitted on the whole computed \
curve, the form misses by 1.2 to 1.7 per cent of the depth."
}], "ItemNumbered",ExpressionUUID->"6d9e844b-dde3-4ccf-a62b-f3f5380b2919"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["The coefficients are not constants of the theory.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["a", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["SF",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["X", "TI"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "da6eaecc-db6d-4c1a-8972-2be0ae3b276a"],
 " differs from the Taylor coefficient at the origin, and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["b", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["SF",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["X", "TI"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2a8e21f4-2f65-4fc2-ac7d-8c76f4a08da5"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["c", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["SF",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["X", "TI"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d782e795-31aa-432d-ac4e-6befebaeb3ee"],
 " change with the fitted interval and with the number of powers (the last \
four rows of the table). No physical meaning may be given to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["b", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["SF",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["X", "TI"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "655352c2-2f80-4f5d-940a-c4fb2f08843b"],
 " or ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["c", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["SF",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["X", "TI"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4792cd96-6fbe-4c29-857a-cbf61e5a6c11"],
 " alone. The physical quantities are those that the computed function \
defines: ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", 
    RowBox[{"0", ",", 
     StyleBox["SF",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]}], 
    StyleBox["X", "TI"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "95f4eb5a-0911-46e6-93c9-2d5361d1bd93"],
 ", the depth, the curvatures at the minimum, and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["a", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["SF",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
     StyleBox["Tay",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]}]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c0c17afc-07da-482a-8759-5310e08a3250"],
 "."
}], "ItemNumbered",ExpressionUUID->"b0d86d43-4001-4069-a559-7da72fb24a83"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["The qualitative results do not depend on the fit.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " That ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[ScriptCapitalV]",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["SF",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["X", "TI"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4928b2bc-99c1-4199-a32c-8d1dfe4403d6"],
 " vanishes at the origin, is negative near it, has its minimum at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", 
    RowBox[{"0", ",", 
     StyleBox["SF",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]}], 
    StyleBox["X", "TI"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "977f2084-12b0-4882-b988-83b344235e7f"],
 ", depends only on the two invariants, and has a stable polar minimum (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["u", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["SF",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox["X", "TI"]], ">", "0"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6a6c3c1a-1272-4e9f-ac84-e963b052eb31"],
 ") are properties of the computed function, checked on it directly; the sign \
of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["a", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["SF",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["X", "TI"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "123bbfc9-5b0a-43db-aa51-ddc2ed66b0c4"],
 " is that of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["a", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["SF",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
     StyleBox["Tay",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]}]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "ed1322d9-0265-4b64-9248-8b7c5ecbd5fd"],
 " (negative: the normal vacuum is unstable)."
}], "ItemNumbered",ExpressionUUID->"309fc11c-52d5-43b5-994d-d39db5f99819"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["The comparison with the Standard Model.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " The field has a Mexican hat with the symmetry structure of the Higgs \
sector and of the polar phase of a condensate of spin 1, but its potential is \
not the quartic potential of the Standard Model: the quartic form misses ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[ScriptCapitalV]",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["SF",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["X", "TI"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5118a6fb-f0b0-4877-b6c4-21b95a574b92"],
 " by 2.8 to 5.9 per cent of the depth, about ten times more than the Landau \
form with the sixth power."
}], "ItemNumbered",ExpressionUUID->"fad7fd29-678a-4adf-8b2a-dd43da30f0ab"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Corrections of the first answers.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " The first answers to the author contained five statements that were not \
exact; the numbers of this chapter are the corrected ones. (1) The residual \
changes its sign three times, not five. (2) The fit called a fit on ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"[", 
    RowBox[{"0", ",", "2", 
     SubscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", "0"]}], "]"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "e46d4e47-db9c-4378-8b1a-e45bb69dcbfe"],
 " used all 61 points of the curve, whose fields reach 1.52 to 1.64 times ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", 
    RowBox[{"0", ",", 
     StyleBox["SF",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]}], 
    StyleBox["X", "TI"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "dfe6dadd-0645-4075-9782-b46ea177e8ec"],
 "; the applied field, not the field of the states, reaches ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"2", 
    SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", 
     RowBox[{"0", ",", 
      StyleBox["SF",
       FontSlant->"Plain"]}], 
     StyleBox["X", "TI"]]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "dd635aa5-c1be-454d-8e13-b6de426e22e8"],
 ". (3) The range of the end of the curve is 1.52 to 1.64 (HS ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{"0", ",", "0"}], ")"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "74b30a60-8bd1-4259-98ee-90f503f2e1cd"],
 "), not 1.52 to 1.61. (4) The singularity lies at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", 
     StyleBox["a",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], "2"], "\[LongEqual]", 
    RowBox[{"-", 
     SuperscriptBox[
      RowBox[{"(", 
       SubsuperscriptBox[
        StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["SF",
         FontSlant->"Plain"], 
        RowBox[{
         StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
         StyleBox["D",
          FontSlant->"Plain"]}]], ")"}], "2"]}]}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "32dbf46b-98b2-4561-ac40-2ec509f01d3d"],
 " in the applied field; in the field of the states the radius of convergence \
is of the order of the Dirac mass, not equal to it. (5) The errors of the \
curvature quoted first, 1.1 to 2.7 per cent, are those of the polynomial at \
the minimum of the computed curve; at the polynomial's own minimum, where a \
user evaluates it, they are 0.86 to 2.3 per cent, as the table shows."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"25d0e680-f079-4df2-ad2b-c7beb80aa365"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["The list of all checks", "Chapter",ExpressionUUID->"b46fd3fa-031b-4480-abec-e74a1cc766c4"],

Cell["\<\
The last cell lists every check of this notebook with its result and its \
counterparts in the Rust and the Python programs, and counts the checks that \
passed.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"eb3fac69-7aac-4f7e-90d8-730f0f5a9c6a"],

